    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/acupoints.owl">
        <dc:contributor>Fahim T. Imam, PhD - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X</dc:contributor>
        <dc:contributor>Ilias Ziogas, PhD - https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9210-2455</dc:contributor>
        <dc:contributor>Maryann E. Martone, PhD - https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8406-3871</dc:contributor>
        <dc:contributor>Richard Harris, PhD - https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2067-8447</dc:contributor>
        <dc:creator>Fahim T. Imam, PhD - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X</dc:creator>
        <dc:date>April 17, 2026</dc:date>
        <dc:description xml:lang="en">The TARA Acupoints Ontology is an ontology developed as part of the Topological Atlas and Repository for Acupoint Research (TARA) project funded by the National Institute of Health (NIH). The goal of TARA is to establish a new comprehensive resource for the acupuncture research and clinician community. The ontology will be used to support semantic search and annotations for anatomical maps, atlases, and data sets relevant to the TARA project.</dc:description>
        <dc:source xml:lang="en">Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dc:source>
        <dc:source xml:lang="en">WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 26. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407</dc:source>
        <dc:title xml:lang="en">TARA Acupoints Ontology</dc:title>
        <rdfs:comment>This file contains the imported terms from InterLex used by the TARA Acupoints Ontology (http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795339). It includes the basic hierarchy and the partnomy of the imported terms. [Latest Update: 2026-07-09]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This file containts imported UBERON terms for the TARA Acupoints Ontology. Generated by import_uberon_terms.py. Hierarchy up to UBERON:0001062 (anatomical entity). CL, GO, NCBITaxon, and PATO classes excluded. OWL axioms: named-class subClassOf BFO:0000050 (part_of), RO_0001025 (located_in), RO_0002170 (connected_to), or BFO_0000051 (has_part) restrictions only.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This file includes an upper-level reference module for the TARA Acupoints Ontology. It contains a subset of the Basic Formal Ontology (BFO) and a minimal subset of object properties from the Relations Ontology (BFO/RO Core). For metadata/annotation properties, it includes a subset of the Information Artifact Ontology (IAO).
- About RO Core: https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/wiki/ROCore
- About BFO: https://obofoundry.org/ontology/bfo.html
- About IAO: https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso xml:lang="en">- About TARA Project: https://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara
- TARA Ontology GitHub Repo: https://purl.org/tara/ontology/repo
- TARA Ontology Updates: https://purl.org/tara/ontology/updates
- TARA Ontology Files: https://purl.org/tara/ontology</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <owl:priorVersion>1.2.0</owl:priorVersion>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.5.0</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


