    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002131"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">is part of</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Every cell nucleus is part_of some cell.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">my brain is part of my body (continuant parthood, two material entities)</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">my stomach cavity is part of my stomach (continuant parthood, immaterial entity is part of material entity)</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this day is part of this year (occurrent parthood)</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A primitive, reflexive, transitive relation holding between two continuants (or, in its occurrent-specific form, between two processes), such that b part_of c holds when, at every time t at which b exists, b is a continuant part of c at t.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a core relation that holds between a part and its whole</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Everything is part of itself. Any part of any part of a thing is itself part of that thing. Two distinct things cannot be part of each other.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Occurrents are not subject to change and so parthood between occurrents holds for all the times that the part exists. Many continuants are subject to change, so parthood between continuants will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Parthood requires the part and the whole to have compatible classes: only an occurrent can be part of an occurrent; only a process can be part of a process; only a continuant can be part of a continuant; only an independent continuant can be part of an independent continuant; only an immaterial entity can be part of an immaterial entity; only a specifically dependent continuant can be part of a specifically dependent continuant; only a generically dependent continuant can be part of a generically dependent continuant. (This list is not exhaustive.)

A continuant cannot be part of an occurrent: use &apos;participates in&apos;. An occurrent cannot be part of a continuant: use &apos;has participant&apos;. A material entity cannot be part of an immaterial entity: use &apos;has location&apos;. A specifically dependent continuant cannot be part of an independent continuant: use &apos;inheres in&apos;. An independent continuant cannot be part of a specifically dependent continuant: use &apos;bearer of&apos;.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Simplified/summary rendering: BFO 2020 formally defines part_of via separate temporalized continuant_part_of and occurrent_part_of relations rather than a single non-temporalized elucidation; this entry gives the commonly cited summary form used across OBO ontologies.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">part_of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 axiom family [002-xxx]; RO core.obo (BFO_0000050 part_of, is_a: RO:0002131 overlaps).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>part of</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">part of</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>http://www.obofoundry.org/ro/#OBO_REL:part_of</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002131"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">has part</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">my body has part my brain (continuant parthood, two material entities)</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">my stomach has part my stomach cavity (continuant parthood, material entity has part immaterial entity)</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this year has part this day (occurrent parthood)</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a core relation that holds between a whole and its part</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Everything has itself as a part. Any part of any part of a thing is itself part of that thing. Two distinct things cannot have each other as a part.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:inverseOf axiom on BFO:0000050 (part_of); not independently used as a TARA property.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Occurrents are not subject to change and so parthood between occurrents holds for all the times that the part exists. Many continuants are subject to change, so parthood between continuants will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Parthood requires the part and the whole to have compatible classes: only an occurrent have an occurrent as part; only a process can have a process as part; only a continuant can have a continuant as part; only an independent continuant can have an independent continuant as part; only a specifically dependent continuant can have a specifically dependent continuant as part; only a generically dependent continuant can have a generically dependent continuant as part. (This list is not exhaustive.)

A continuant cannot have an occurrent as part: use &apos;participates in&apos;. An occurrent cannot have a continuant as part: use &apos;has participant&apos;. An immaterial entity cannot have a material entity as part: use &apos;location of&apos;. An independent continuant cannot have a specifically dependent continuant as part: use &apos;bearer of&apos;. A specifically dependent continuant cannot have an independent continuant as part: use &apos;inheres in&apos;.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">has_part</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>has part</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has part</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000066 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000066">
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000067"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000003"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000066"/>
        </owl:propertyChainAxiom>
        <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000066"/>
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
        </owl:propertyChainAxiom>
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">occurs in</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">b occurs_in c =def b is a process and c is a material entity or immaterial entity&amp; there exists a spatiotemporal region r and b occupies_spatiotemporal_region r.&amp; forall(t) if b exists_at t then c exists_at t &amp; there exist spatial regions s and s’ where &amp; b spatially_projects_onto s at t&amp; c is occupies_spatial_region s’ at t&amp; s is a proper_continuant_part_of s’ at t</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">occurs_in</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">unfolds in</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">unfolds_in</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:comment>Paraphrase of definition: a relation between a process and an independent continuant, in which the process takes place entirely within the independent continuant</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">occurs in</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000067 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000067">
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">site of</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">[copied from inverse property &apos;occurs in&apos;] b occurs_in c =def b is a process and c is a material entity or immaterial entity&amp; there exists a spatiotemporal region r and b occupies_spatiotemporal_region r.&amp; forall(t) if b exists_at t then c exists_at t &amp; there exist spatial regions s and s’ where &amp; b spatially_projects_onto s at t&amp; c is occupies_spatial_region s’ at t&amp; s is a proper_continuant_part_of s’ at t</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>Paraphrase of definition: a relation between an independent continuant and a process, in which the process takes place entirely within the independent continuant</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">contains process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is about</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000052 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000052">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000111>characteristic of</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">inheres in</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>This red color inheres in this apple. This fragility inheres in this vase.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this fragility is a characteristic of this vase</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this red color is a characteristic of this apple</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A relation between a specifically dependent continuant (the characteristic) and any other entity (the bearer), in which the characteristic depends on the bearer for its existence.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a relation between a specifically dependent continuant (the characteristic) and any other entity (the bearer), in which the characteristic depends on the bearer for its existence.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>IMPORTANT: RO renamed this term&apos;s preferred label from &apos;inheres in&apos; to &apos;characteristic of&apos; in its 2021-03-08 release, and correspondingly relaxed its definition (the bearer need no longer be an independent continuant). BFO 2020 retains a separate, more restricted native relation, BFO:0000197 (inheres in), for the classic independent-continuant-bearer case. TARA&apos;s tara-op:isSpecialPointDesignationOf (reserved, not currently populated) was originally modeled against the older, narrower &apos;inheres in&apos; reading of this ID; if that reserved property is ever activated, switching its superproperty to BFO:0000197 would better match current upstream terminology.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">inheres_in</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>OBO Relations Ontology (RO) core.obo, RO:0000052 &apos;characteristic of&apos; (formerly &apos;inheres in&apos;).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Note that this relation was previously called &quot;inheres in&quot;, but was changed to be called &quot;characteristic of&quot; because BFO2 uses &quot;inheres in&quot; in a more restricted fashion. This relation differs from BFO2:inheres_in in two respects: (1) it does not impose a range constraint, and thus it allows qualities of processes, as well as of information entities, whereas BFO2 restricts inheres_in to only apply to independent continuants (2) it is declared functional, i.e. something can only be a characteristic of one thing.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">characteristic of</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#InverseFunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">bearer of</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>This apple is bearer of this red color. This vase is bearer of this fragility.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this apple is bearer of this red color</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this vase is bearer of this fragility</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a specifically dependent continuant (the dependent), in which the dependent specifically depends on the bearer for its existence.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Inverse of characteristic_of</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">A bearer can have many dependents, and its dependents can exist for different periods of time, but none of its dependents can exist when the bearer does not exist.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>A bearer can have many dependents, and its dependents can exist for different periods of time, but none of its dependents can exist when the bearer does not exist. In TARA this is the reserved superproperty of tara-op:hasSpecialPointDesignation (not currently populated); see also RO:0000087 (has_role), the more specific subproperty actually used for tara-op:hasSpecialPointRole.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">bearer_of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">is bearer of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has characteristic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000079 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000079">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000052"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000085"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this catalysis function is a function of this enzyme</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a relation between a function and an independent continuant (the bearer), in which the function specifically depends on the bearer for its existence</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">A function inheres in its bearer at all times for which the function exists, however the function need not be realized at all the times that the function exists.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">function_of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">is function of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:comment>This relation is modeled after the BFO relation of the same name which was in BFO2, but is used in a more restricted sense - specifically, we model this relation as functional (inherited from characteristic-of). Note that this relation is now removed from BFO2020.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">function of</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000052"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this red color is a quality of this apple</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a relation between a quality and an independent continuant (the bearer), in which the quality specifically depends on the bearer for its existence</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">A quality inheres in its bearer at all times for which the quality exists.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">is quality of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">quality_of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:comment>This relation is modeled after the BFO relation of the same name which was in BFO2, but is used in a more restricted sense - specifically, we model this relation as functional (inherited from characteristic-of). Note that this relation is now removed from BFO2020.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">quality of</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000081 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000081">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000052"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>This investigator role is role of this person. Front-Mu Point of the Lung Role isSpecialPointRoleOf LU1.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this investigator role is a role of this person</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A relation between a role and the independent continuant that bears it, in which the role specifically depends on the bearer for its existence; the inverse of has_role (RO:0000087).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a relation between a role and an independent continuant (the bearer), in which the role specifically depends on the bearer for its existence</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">A role inheres in its bearer at all times for which the role exists, however the role need not be realized at all the times that the role exists.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Presented here by symmetry with RO:0000087 (has_role), of which it is the formal inverse; a verbatim RO source record for this specific ID&apos;s definition text could not be independently confirmed at time of writing, so this entry should be checked against the live RO release before being treated as an exact quotation.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">is role of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">role_of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl"/>
        <rdfs:comment>This relation is modeled after the BFO relation of the same name which was in BFO2, but is used in a more restricted sense - specifically, we model this relation as functional (inherited from characteristic-of). Note that this relation is now removed from BFO2020.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>role of</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">role of</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000085 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000085">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this enzyme has function this catalysis function (more colloquially: this enzyme has this catalysis function)</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a function, in which the function specifically depends on the bearer for its existence</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">A bearer can have many functions, and its functions can exist for different periods of time, but none of its functions can exist when the bearer does not exist. A function need not be realized at all the times that the function exists.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">has_function</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has function</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this apple has quality this red color</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a quality, in which the quality specifically depends on the bearer for its existence</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">A bearer can have many qualities, and its qualities can exist for different periods of time, but none of its qualities can exist when the bearer does not exist.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">has_quality</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has quality</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>This person has role this investigator role. LU1 hasSpecialPointRole Front-Mu Point of the Lung Role.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a role, in which the role specifically depends on the bearer for its existence.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">A bearer can have many roles, and its roles can exist for different periods of time, but none of its roles can exist when the bearer does not exist. A role need not be realized at all the times that the role exists.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">has_role</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000091 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000091">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000092"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a disposition, in which the disposition specifically depends on the bearer for its existence</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has disposition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000092 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000092">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000052"/>
        <rdfs:comment>This relation is modeled after the BFO relation of the same name which was in BFO2, but is used in a more restricted sense - specifically, we model this relation as functional (inherited from characteristic-of). Note that this relation is now removed from BFO2020.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">disposition of</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001015 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001015">
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">is location of</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">my head is the location of my brain</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this cage is the location of this rat</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a relation between two independent continuants, the location and the target, in which the target is entirely within the location</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Most location relations will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">location of</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <rdfs:domain>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:complementOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006"/>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:domain>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <rdfs:range>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:complementOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006"/>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:range>
        <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025"/>
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
        </owl:propertyChainAxiom>
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">located in</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">my brain is located in my head</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this rat is located in this cage</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>c is located_in c1 (at a time t) if and only if the spatial region occupied by c is part_of the spatial region occupied by c1 (at t). This relation comprehends both exact location (as when a portion of fluid exactly fills a cavity) and inexact/containment-style location (as between brain and head, or ovum and uterus).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Chosen over overlaps (RO:0002131) for the Acupoint surface-anatomy and meridian relations because located_in does not require the two related continuants to be of the same BFO category (material vs. immaterial), unlike overlaps, which requires a literal shared part. The property-chain axiom (located_in o part_of -&gt; located_in) means that if c is located_in c1 and c1 is part_of c2, then c is automatically inferred located_in c2 as well.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Location as a relation between instances: The primitive instance-level relation c located_in r at t reflects the fact that each continuant is at any given time associated with exactly one spatial region, namely its exact location. Following we can use this relation to define a further instance-level location relation - not between a continuant and the region which it exactly occupies, but rather between one continuant and another. c is located in c1, in this sense, whenever the spatial region occupied by c is part_of the spatial region occupied by c1.    Note that this relation comprehends both the relation of exact location between one continuant and another which obtains when r and r1 are identical (for example, when a portion of fluid exactly fills a cavity), as well as those sorts of inexact location relations which obtain, for example, between brain and head or between ovum and uterus</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Most location relations will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">located_in</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl"/>
        <dcterms:source>http://www.obofoundry.org/ro/#OBO_REL:located_in</dcterms:source>
        <rdfs:label>located in</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">located in</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>This is redundant with the more specific &apos;independent and not spatial region&apos; constraint. We leave in the redundant axiom for use with reasoners that do not use negation.</obo:IAO_0000116>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>This is redundant with the more specific &apos;independent and not spatial region&apos; constraint. We leave in the redundant axiom for use with reasoners that do not use negation.</obo:IAO_0000116>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002131 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002131">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#SymmetricProperty"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy Axillary Artery.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>x overlaps y if and only if there exists some z such that x has part z and z part of y.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>part_of (BFO:0000050) is itself a subproperty of overlaps in RO&apos;s own hierarchy (is_a: RO:0002131 overlaps), since anything that is part_of something automatically overlaps it -- this is why overlaps, not part_of, is the true root of this branch.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>overlaps</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002170 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002170">
        <rdfs:label>connected to</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">connected to</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002350 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002350">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002351"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>An organism that is a member of a population of organisms</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>is member of is a mereological relation between a item and a collection.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>is member of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>member part of</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>SIO</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">member of</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002351 -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002351">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>has member is a mereological relation between a collection and an item.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>SIO</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has member</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasAssociatedOrgan -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasAssociatedOrgan">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7226516"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Lung Meridian hasAssociatedOrgan Lung.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Meridian a hasAssociatedOrgan an organ b if and only if traditional Chinese medicine theory designates b as the organ system with which a is affiliated.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates a Meridian to the organ it is associated with according to traditional Chinese medicine theory (e.g., Lung Meridian hasAssociatedOrgan Lung). Used to express the organ affiliation of a meridian as an OWL axiom.</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Not declared as a subproperty of any RO relation, because the organ affiliation of a meridian is a doctrinal/functional association defined by TCM theory rather than a spatial or mereological relationship; located_in, overlaps, and part_of do not accurately describe it, so the property is left ungrounded at the top of the object-property hierarchy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasAssociatedOrgan</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasGeneralSurfaceLocation -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasGeneralSurfaceLocation">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasGeneralSurfaceLocation Anterior Thoracic Region.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasGeneralSurfaceLocation a region b if and only if a hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy b, and b is the coarse-grained body region within which a is situated.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint to the general body region on whose surface it is located (e.g., LU 1 hasGeneralSurfaceLocation Anterior Thoracic Region). It provides a coarse-grained anatomical grouping for the acupoint and is used together with hasSpecificSurfaceLocation, which further specifies particular anatomical landmarks within this general region.</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Inherits its subproperty-of relation to RO:0001025 (located_in) from its parent property hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy; rdfs:subPropertyOf is transitive, so no separate RO assertion is required here.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasGeneralSurfaceLocation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedArtery -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedArtery">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedVasculature"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasRelatedArtery Axillary Artery.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasRelatedArtery an artery b if and only if a hasRelatedVasculature b and b is a UBERON:0001637 artery.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint directly to a specific artery occupying its location (e.g., LU 1 hasRelatedArtery Axillary Artery, Thoracoacromial Artery).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Inherits its subproperty-of relation to RO:0002131 (overlaps) from its ancestor properties hasRelatedVasculature and hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy; rdfs:subPropertyOf is transitive, so no separate RO assertion is required here.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasRelatedArtery</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedInnervation -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedInnervation">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasRelatedInnervation Intermediate Supraclavicular Nerve.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasRelatedInnervation a nerve b if and only if a hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy b.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint to the nerve(s) supplying the tissue at its location, relevant to safe needling (e.g., LU 1 hasRelatedInnervation Intermediate Supraclavicular Nerve).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Inherits its subproperty-of relation to RO:0002131 (overlaps) from its parent property hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy; rdfs:subPropertyOf is transitive, so no separate RO assertion is required here.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasRelatedInnervation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedNerve -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedNerve">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedInnervation"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasRelatedNerve Intermediate Supraclavicular Nerve.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasRelatedNerve a nerve b if and only if a hasRelatedInnervation b and b is a UBERON:0001021 nerve.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint directly to a specific nerve occupying its location (e.g., LU 1 hasRelatedNerve Intermediate Supraclavicular Nerve, Anterior Thoracic Nerve, Lateral Cutaneous Branch of First Intercostal Nerve).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Inherits its subproperty-of relation to RO:0002131 (overlaps) from its ancestor properties hasRelatedInnervation and hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy; rdfs:subPropertyOf is transitive, so no separate RO assertion is required here.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasRelatedNerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002131"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasTopographicalAnatomy"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy Axillary Artery.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy a material anatomical entity b if and only if a overlaps b, where b is a nerve, artery, or vein occupying the fiat volume of a.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint to the nerves, arteries, and veins that occupy the same shallow tissue volume as the acupoint at the site of needle insertion (e.g., LU 1 hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy Axillary Artery, Axillary Vein, Intermediate Supraclavicular Nerve).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Declared as a subproperty of RO:0002131 (overlaps) because an Acupoint, modeled as a BFO:0000024 Fiat Object Part, and the nerves/vessels beneath it are both material entities; the segment of the nerve or vessel passing through the acupoint&apos;s fiat volume is a literal shared part, satisfying overlaps&apos; requirement of a common part between the two continuants.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasTopographicalAnatomy"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy Anterior Thoracic Region.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy an anatomical entity b if and only if a is located_in b, where b is a surface-level anatomical region, landmark, fossa, or line used to describe the position of a on the body surface.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint to an anatomical region, fossa, line, or other surface landmark in the vicinity of its location on the body surface (e.g., LU 1 hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy Anterior Thoracic Region, Infraclavicular Fossa, and Anterior Median Line).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Declared as a subproperty of RO:0001025 (located_in) rather than RO:0002131 (overlaps), because the anatomical entities used to describe surface location (e.g., regions, fossae, lines) span a mix of material and immaterial UBERON classes; located_in does not require the related entities to share a common part, so it remains valid across this mixed range, unlike overlaps.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedVasculature -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedVasculature">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasRelatedVasculature Axillary Artery.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasRelatedVasculature a vessel b if and only if a hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy b.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint to the blood vessel(s) present at its location, relevant to safe needling (e.g., LU 1 hasRelatedVasculature Axillary Artery, Axillary Vein, Thoracoacromial Artery, Thoracoacromial Vein).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Inherits its subproperty-of relation to RO:0002131 (overlaps) from its parent property hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy; rdfs:subPropertyOf is transitive, so no separate RO assertion is required here.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasRelatedVasculature</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedVein -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedVein">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedVasculature"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasRelatedVein Axillary Vein.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasRelatedVein a vein b if and only if a hasRelatedVasculature b and b is a UBERON:0001638 vein.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint directly to a specific vein occupying its location (e.g., LU 1 hasRelatedVein Axillary Vein, Thoracoacromial Vein).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Inherits its subproperty-of relation to RO:0002131 (overlaps) from its ancestor properties hasRelatedVasculature and hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy; rdfs:subPropertyOf is transitive, so no separate RO assertion is required here.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasRelatedVein</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasSpecialPointDesignation -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasSpecialPointDesignation">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/isSpecialPointDesignationOf"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Reserved; not currently asserted. If used: LU1 hasSpecialPointDesignation Front-Mu Point of the Lung Role.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasSpecialPointDesignation a role class b if and only if a is designated, according to traditional Chinese medicine sources, as bearing the special role b -- a relation currently intended to be logically equivalent to hasSpecialPointRole but not yet populated in this ontology.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property, reserved for potential future use, that would relate an Acupoint to its designated special acupoint role class (e.g., LU 1 hasSpecialPointDesignation Front-Mu Point of the Lung Role). It is not currently asserted on any Acupoint individual in this ontology; hasSpecialPointRole is the property actually used to classify Acupoints as Special Points. It is retained in the property hierarchy for possible future use, e.g., to distinguish a recorded designation from the realized role.</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Declared as a subproperty of RO:0000053 (bearer_of), the general relation between an independent continuant and any realizable entity, rather than RO:0000087 (has_role), to leave open a possible future distinction between &apos;is designated as&apos; and &apos;has the realized role of&apos; without prematurely committing to role semantics; not currently used in this ontology.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasSpecialPointDesignation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasSpecialPointRole -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasSpecialPointRole">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/isSpecialPointRoleOf"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4176111"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasSpecialPointRole Front-Mu Point of the Lung Role.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasSpecialPointRole a role b if and only if a has_role b, where b is a Special_Acupoint_Role realized in acupuncture practice.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint to the special role it bears (e.g., LU 1 hasSpecialPointRole Front-Mu Point of the Lung Role). It is the inverse of isSpecialPointRoleOf and is the sole property used in this ontology to assert special-point classification for Acupoints.</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Declared as a subproperty of RO:0000087 (has_role) rather than the more generic RO:0000053 (bearer_of), because its range is specifically restricted to instances of Special_Acupoint_Role, a subclass of BFO:0000023 Role; has_role is the RO relation specific to realizable entities of type Role, giving a more precise commitment than the fully general bearer_of.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasSpecialPointRole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasSpecificSurfaceLocation -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasSpecificSurfaceLocation">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasSpecificSurfaceLocation Infraclavicular Fossa.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a hasSpecificSurfaceLocation a landmark b if and only if a hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy b, and b is a specific anatomical landmark, fossa, or line used to further localize a within its general surface region.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint to one or more specific anatomical landmarks within the general body region identified by hasGeneralSurfaceLocation, providing a finer-grained localization of the acupoint (e.g., LU 1 hasSpecificSurfaceLocation First Intercostal Space, Infraclavicular Fossa, and Anterior Median Line).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Inherits its subproperty-of relation to RO:0001025 (located_in) from its parent property hasRelatedSurfaceAnatomy; rdfs:subPropertyOf is transitive, so no separate RO assertion is required here.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasSpecificSurfaceLocation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasTopographicalAnatomy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/hasTopographicalAnatomy">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 hasTopographicalAnatomy Anterior Thoracic Region. LU1 hasTopographicalAnatomy Axillary Artery.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A grouping relation between an Acupoint and any anatomical entity related to its surface or subsurface topography, holding whenever a more specific subproperty of hasTopographicalAnatomy holds between the same two entities.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that groups all relations between an Acupoint and the surface and subsurface anatomical entities associated with its location and needling, including surface regions, landmarks, nerves, arteries, and veins. It is the root organizational property for the Acupoint topographical-anatomy property hierarchy and carries no independent logical commitment of its own.</dc:description>
        <tara:hasSynonym>hasRegionalAnatomy</tara:hasSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Declared as a direct subproperty of owl:topObjectProperty rather than of any RO relation, because it is used purely to organize the Acupoint-specific property hierarchy for browsing and querying and does not itself assert overlap, location, or any other specific spatial relationship; that logical content is carried entirely by its subproperties.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>hasTopographicalAnatomy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/isLocatedOnMeridian -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/isLocatedOnMeridian">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7226516"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>LU1 isLocatedOnMeridian Lung Meridian.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint a isLocatedOnMeridian a Meridian b if and only if a is located_in b, where b is the one-dimensional fiat channel along which a is conventionally situated.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates an Acupoint to the Meridian along which it is located (e.g., LU 1 isLocatedOnMeridian Lung Meridian).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Declared as a subproperty of RO:0001025 (located_in) rather than RO:0002350 (member_of), because a Meridian is modeled as a BFO:0000009 one-dimensional continuant fiat boundary -- a channel that acupoints are located along -- rather than as an aggregate whose identity is exhausted by the sum of its acupoints; located_in correctly expresses this geometric relationship without implying that the meridian is merely a collection of its acupoints.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>isLocatedOnMeridian</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/isSpecialPointDesignationOf -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/isSpecialPointDesignationOf">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000052"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4176111"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Reserved; not currently asserted.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A role a isSpecialPointDesignationOf an Acupoint b if and only if b hasSpecialPointDesignation a.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property, reserved for potential future use, that would relate a special acupoint role to the Acupoint designated to bear it. It is the inverse of hasSpecialPointDesignation and is not currently asserted on any individual in this ontology.</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Declared as a subproperty of RO:0000052 (inheres_in), consistent with hasSpecialPointDesignation being a subproperty of the general RO:0000053 (bearer_of); reserved and not currently used.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>isSpecialPointDesignationOf</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/isSpecialPointRoleOf -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/object-property/isSpecialPointRoleOf">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000081"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4176111"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1132428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Front-Mu Point of the Lung Role isSpecialPointRoleOf LU1.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A role a isSpecialPointRoleOf an Acupoint b if and only if b hasSpecialPointRole a.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>An object property that relates a special acupoint role to the Acupoint that bears it (e.g., Front-Mu Point of the Lung Role isSpecialPointRoleOf LU 1). It is the inverse of hasSpecialPointRole.</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Declared as a subproperty of RO:0000081 (role_of) as the inverse counterpart of has_role, consistent with hasSpecialPointRole being a subproperty of RO:0000087 (has_role).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>isSpecialPointRoleOf</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Data properties
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000004 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000004">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has measurement value</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000404 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000404">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has x coordinate value</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000405 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000405">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has z coordinate value</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000406 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000406">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has y coordinate value</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Classes
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An entity is anything that exists or has existed or will exist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>&apos;Entity&apos; is a primitive term: it is so basic to our understanding of reality that there is no way of defining it non-circularly, so BFO supplies only an elucidation rather than a genus-differentia definition. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [001-001])</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021), axiom [001-001].</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000002">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000003"/>
        <owl:disjointWith>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000003"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </owl:disjointWith>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>An organism; a heart; a color; a role; the sequence of a protein molecule.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An entity that exists in full at any time in which it exists at all, persists through time while maintaining its identity and has no temporal parts.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>continuant</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000003">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001"/>
        <owl:disjointWith>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000002"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </owl:disjointWith>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An entity that has temporal parts and that happens, unfolds or develops through time.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:disjointWith axiom on BFO:0000002 (continuant), which reflects BFO&apos;s fundamental continuant/occurrent bifurcation; not independently used as a TARA class.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>occurrent</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000002"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>An organism; a heart; a chair; a spatial region.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">b is an independent continuant = Def. b is a continuant which is such that there is no c and no t such that b s-depends_on c at t. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [017-002])</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021); disjointness with specifically/generically dependent continuant confirmed against the BFO OBO source (BFO_0000004 disjoint_from: BFO_0000020, BFO_0000031).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A continuant that is a bearer of quality and realizable entity entities, in which other entities inhere and which itself cannot inhere in anything.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>independent continuant</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:disjointWith axiom on BFO:0000140 (continuant fiat boundary); not independently used as a TARA class.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>spatial region</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000018"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>The Equator; all geopolitical boundaries; all lines of latitude and longitude; the median sulcus of the tongue; the line separating the outer surface of the mucosa of the lower lip from the outer surface of the skin of the chin.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>(Elucidation, reconstructed by analogy with the confirmed BFO definitions of the sibling zero- and two-dimensional continuant fiat boundary classes) A one-dimensional continuant fiat boundary (line) is a self-connected fiat line whose location is defined in relation to some material entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>TARA:Meridian is modeled as a subclass of this class: a TCM meridian is a channel/line demarcated by convention within acupuncture theory, not by any natural physical discontinuity, matching the fiat-line character of this class&apos;s own examples (e.g. the Equator, lines of latitude/longitude). NOTE: the exact verbatim BFO source text for this specific class&apos;s elucidation could not be independently confirmed at time of writing (unlike its zero- and two-dimensional siblings, which were confirmed verbatim); the definition given here is a faithful reconstruction by direct analogy and should be checked against the live BFO OWL release. The example list, however, is drawn directly from a confirmed source.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021), axiom family [031-032].</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>one-dimensional continuant fiat boundary</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000003"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">p is a process = Def. p is an occurrent that has temporal proper parts and for some time t, p s-depends_on some material entity at t. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [083-003])</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An occurrent that has temporal proper parts and for some time t, p s-depends_on some material entity at t.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:disjointWith axiom on BFO:0000023 (role). Directly relevant to TARA&apos;s design history: the Role/Disposition distinction (a role depends on external context; a disposition depends on the bearer&apos;s own physical make-up) is exactly the criterion used to justify modeling TARA:Special_Acupoint_Role as a Role rather than a Disposition.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>disposition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>The role of being a doctor; the function of your reproductive organs; the disposition of your blood to coagulate; the disposition of a piece of metal to conduct electricity.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A specifically dependent continuant  that inheres in continuant  entities and are not exhibited in full at every time in which it inheres in an entity or group of entities. The exhibition or actualization of a realizable entity is a particular manifestation, functioning or process that occurs under certain circumstances.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Distinguished from quality (the other main subtype of specifically dependent continuant) by the fact that a realizable entity need not be manifested/realized at every time it exists (e.g. a role can exist unrealized), whereas a quality is fully manifested whenever it is borne at all.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>realizable entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000018 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000018">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:disjointWith axiom on BFO:0000009 (one-dimensional continuant fiat boundary). Directly relevant to TARA&apos;s design history: this class (a dimensionless fiat point) was the very first alternative considered and rejected for TARA:Acupoint, since a 0-D boundary cannot have parts and so cannot overlap material nerves/vessels.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>zero-dimensional continuant fiat boundary</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:disjointWith axiom on BFO:0000017 (realizable entity); not independently used as a TARA class.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>quality</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000002"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>A color; a shape; a role; a disposition.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">b is a specifically dependent continuant = Def. b is a continuant &amp; there is some independent continuant c which is not a spatial region and which is such that b s-depends_on c at every time t during the course of b’s existence. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [050-003])</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A continuant that inheres in or is borne by other entities. Every instance of A requires some specific instance of B which must always be the same.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>specifically dependent continuant</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>The priest role; the student role; the role of subject in a clinical trial; the role of a stone in marking a property boundary; the role of a building in serving as a military target.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>(Elucidation) A role is a realizable entity that exists because there is some single bearer that is in some special physical, social, or institutional set of circumstances in which this bearer does not have to be, and is not such that, if it ceases to exist, then the physical make-up of the bearer is thereby changed.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A realizable entity  the manifestation of which brings about some result or end that is not essential to a continuant  in virtue of the kind of thing that it is but that can be served or participated in by that kind of continuant  in some kinds of natural, social or institutional contexts.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>TARA:Special_Acupoint_Role is modeled as a subclass of this class: whether an acupoint counts as, e.g., a Front-Mu point is conferred entirely by TCM theory (an external, institutional/doctrinal context) rather than by the acupoint&apos;s own physical make-up, matching the defining Role/Disposition distinction given here.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000024 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000024">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000030"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>The upper and lower lobes of the left lung; the dorsal and ventral surfaces of the body; the Western hemisphere of the Earth; the FMA regional parts of an intact human body.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>(Elucidation) A fiat object part b is a material entity which is such that for all times t, if b exists at t then there is some object c such that b is a proper continuant part of c at t and b is demarcated from the remainder of c by one or more fiat surfaces.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>TARA:Acupoint is modeled as a subclass of this class: an acupoint is a fiat-demarcated volume of pre-existing tissue (skin, fascia, muscle), delimited by needling convention rather than by any natural physical discontinuity, matching the &apos;not itself a distinct kind of tissue&apos; character of this class&apos;s own examples (e.g. the upper/lower lobes of the lung are not a distinct tissue type from the rest of the lung).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>fiat object part</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:disjointWith axiom on BFO:0000024 (fiat object part); not independently used as a TARA class.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>object aggregate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000029 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000029">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:disjointWith axiom on BFO:0000140 (continuant fiat boundary). Directly relevant to TARA&apos;s design history: Site was an alternative BFO class considered and rejected for both TARA:Acupoint and TARA:Meridian, precisely because a Site (unlike a Fiat Object Part or a Continuant Fiat Boundary) is immaterial and so cannot overlap the material nerves/vessels those classes need to relate to.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>site</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000030 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000030">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:disjointWith axiom on BFO:0000024 (fiat object part), one of the three (pairwise disjoint) direct subclasses of material entity; not independently used as a TARA class.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>object</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000002"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">b is a generically dependent continuant = Def. b is a continuant that g-depends_on one or more other entities.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry disjointWith axioms against BFO:0000004 and BFO:0000020, the two other direct subclasses of continuant; not independently used as a TARA class.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021), axiom [074-001].</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A continuant that is dependent on one or other independent continuant bearers. For every instance of A requires some instance of (an independent continuant type) B but which instance of B serves can change from time to time.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>generically dependent continuant</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000034 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000034">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"/>
        <rdfs:label>function</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>An organism; a heart; a chair; a lung; an apple.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An independent continuant that is spatially extended whose identity is independent of that of other entities and can be maintained through time.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>material entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>The North Pole (a fiat point); the Equator (a fiat line); the plane separating the Northern from the Southern hemisphere (a fiat surface).</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>b is a continuant fiat boundary = Def. b is an immaterial entity that is of zero, one or two dimensions and does not include a spatial region as part. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [029-001])</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021), axiom [029-001].</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>continuant fiat boundary</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>A spatial region; a site; a continuant fiat boundary.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>b is an immaterial entity =Def. b is an independent continuant which is such that there is no time t when it has a material entity as continuant part.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>immaterial entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Included as a bare stub solely to carry the owl:disjointWith axiom on BFO:0000009 (one-dimensional continuant fiat boundary); not independently used as a TARA class.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>two-dimensional continuant fiat boundary</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000013 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000013">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000088"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000311"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">Examples are articles published in the journals, Nature and Science. The content can often be cited by reference to a paper based encoding, e.g. Authors, Title of article, Journal name, date or year of publication, volume and page number.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A report that is published in a journal.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119 xml:lang="en">group:OBI; OBI_0000159</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 xml:lang="en">http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao.owl</obo:IAO_0000412>
        <rdfs:label>journal article</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">Data items include counts of things, analyte concentrations, and statistical summaries.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An information content entity that is intended to be one or more truthful statement(s) about something (modulo, e.g., measurement precision or other systematic errors) and is constructed/acquired by a method which reliably tends to produce (approximately) truthful statements.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000412>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao.owl</obo:IAO_0000412>
        <rdfs:label>data entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">Examples of information content entites include journal articles, data, graphical layouts, and graphs.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A generically dependent continuant that is about some thing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">2014-03-10: The use of &quot;thing&quot; is intended to be general enough to include universals and configurations (see https://groups.google.com/d/msg/information-ontology/GBxvYZCk1oc/-L6B5fSBBTQJ).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">information_content_entity &apos;is_encoded_in&apos; some digital_entity in obi before split (040907). information_content_entity &apos;is_encoded_in&apos; some physical_document in obi before split (040907). Previous. An information content entity is a non-realizable information entity that &apos;is encoded in&apos; some digital or physical entity.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119 xml:lang="en">OBI_0000142</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao.owl</obo:IAO_0000412>
        <rdfs:label>information content entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000088 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000088">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000310"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">Examples of reports are gene lists and investigation reports. These are not published (journal) articles but may be included in a journal article.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A document assembled by an author for the purpose of providing information for the audience. A report is the output of a documenting process and has the objective to be consumed by a specific audience. Topic of the report is on something that has completed. A report is not a single figure. Examples of reports are journal article, patent application, grant progress report, case report (not patient record).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119 xml:lang="en">GROUP: OBI; OBI_0000099</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 xml:lang="en">http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao.owl</obo:IAO_0000412>
        <rdfs:label>report</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000102 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000102">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Data about an ontology part is a data item about a part of an ontology, for example a term.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000412>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao.owl</obo:IAO_0000412>
        <rdfs:label>data about an ontology part</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000310 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000310">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">A journal article, patent application, laboratory notebook, or a book.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A collection of information content entities intended to be understood together as a whole.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 xml:lang="en">http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao.owl</obo:IAO_0000412>
        <rdfs:label>document</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000311 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000311">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000310"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">journal article, newspaper story, book, etc.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A document that is the output of a publishing process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 xml:lang="en">http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao.owl</obo:IAO_0000412>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Revisit the term in Octorber 2020. Improve the defintion.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>publication</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000312 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000312">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000311"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 xml:lang="en">http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao.owl</obo:IAO_0000412>
        <rdfs:label>publication about an investigation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000003">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000161"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000033"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005725"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Orifice of the olfactory system. The naris is the route by which odorants enter the olfactory system[MAH].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>AAO:0000311</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0001225</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA:9083</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:17847</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0000282</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:272650008</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>VHOG:0000663</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>galen:Naris</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>naris</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000004">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002268"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004121"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The olfactory organ of vertebrates, consisting of nares, olfactory epithelia and the structures and skeletal framework of the nasal cavity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0000840</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>CALOHA:TS-2037</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0001274</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA:1502</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:16542</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EV:0100037</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EV:0100370</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:46472</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
