            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The main trunk of the systemic arterial system that carries blood from the heart to all the organs and other structures of the body, bringing oxygenated blood to all parts of the body in the systemic circulation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>This class is currently a mixed bag, encompassing (1) the entirety of the mammalian aorta together with (2) the developmental and phylogenetic homologs of its segments: the ventral aorta and dorsal aortae.</obo:IAO_0000116>
