    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000950 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000950">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004252"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011144"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000376"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The most superficial muscle on the medial side of the thigh. It is thin and flattened, broad above, narrow and tapering below. It arises by a thin aponeurosis from the anterior margins of the lower half of the symphysis pubis and the upper half of the pubic arch.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>AAO has minor and major gracilis, which merge together, attaching the pelvic rim to the tibiofibula - this could be grouped with the mammalian gracilis at some level; note the current insertion site is &apos;tibia&apos; which would be modified for amphibian tibiafibula</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0000536</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:36231</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:43882</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0002311</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C52935</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:181689005</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C0224439</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Gracilis_muscle</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>galen:Gracilis</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>gracilis muscle</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>musculus gracilis</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>gracilis</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:depiction rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/Anterior_Hip_Muscles_2.PNG</foaf:depiction>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000962 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000962">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001780"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The cervical nerves are the spinal nerves from the cervical vertebrae. Although there are seven cervical vertebrae (C1-C7), there are eight cervical nerves (C1-C8). All nerves except C8 emerge above their corresponding vertebrae, while the C8 nerve emerges below the C7 vertebra. (In the other portions of the spine, the nerve emerges below the vertebra with the same name. Dorsal (posterior) distribution includes the greater occipital (C2) and third occipital (C3). Ventral (anterior) distribution includes the cervical plexus (C1-C4) and brachial plexus (C5-C8) [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:cern</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:5859</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C32299</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>NLXANAT:20090207</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:360497008</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C0228815</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Cervical_nerves</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>neuronames:2351</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>cervical nerve</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>cervical nerve tree</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>cervical spinal nerve</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>nervus cervicalis</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Innervates: sternohyoid muscle, sternothyroid muscle, omohyoid muscle[WP]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>nerve of cervical vertebra</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:depiction rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/Gray795.png</foaf:depiction>
    </owl:Class>
    


