    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001308 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001308">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005609"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001191"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The external iliac artery is a large artery in the pelvic region that carries blood to the lower limb. The external iliac artery is a paired artery, meaning there is one on each side of the body: a right external iliac artery and left external iliac artery. The external iliac artery is accompanied by the external iliac vein, which is located posterior to the artery. [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0004666</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0000463</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA:4337</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:17614</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:18805</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0001973</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C32558</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:181352000</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C0226398</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:External_iliac_artery</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>galen:ExternalIliacArtery</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>arteria iliaca externa</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>external iliac artery</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:depiction rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3e/Gray539.png</foaf:depiction>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001316 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001316">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005610"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002170"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001139"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A large vein that connects the femoral vein to the common iliac vein. Their origin is at the inferior margin of the inguinal ligaments and they terminate when they join the internal iliac veins (to form the common iliac veins). Both external iliac veins are accompanied along their course by external iliac arteries. [WP,modified].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0000464</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:37144</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:18883</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0002144</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C32560</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:181400000</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C0226761</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:External_iliac_vein</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>galen:ExternalIliacVein</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>vena iliaca externa</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>external iliac vein</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:depiction rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://cdn.humanatlas.io/digital-objects/ref-organ/blood-vasculature-male/v1.3/assets/3d-vh-m-blood-vasculature.glb</foaf:depiction>
