    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001374 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001374">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002463"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The biceps femoris is a muscle of the posterior (the back) thigh. As its name implies, it has two parts, one of which (the long head) forms part of the hamstrings muscle group. [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
