        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C0027342</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>VHOG:0001361</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Nail_(anatomy)</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>galen:Nail</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>nail/claw</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>claw</OboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>talon</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>The nails of humans and the claws are moth are highly similar. Both species have a proximal nail fold, cuticle, nail matrix, nail bed, nail plate, and hyponychium. Distinguishing features are the shape of the nail and the presence of an extended hyponychium in the mouse [PMC3579226]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>nail</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


