        <OboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>malleolar bone</OboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>malleolar bone of ankle</OboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>distal extremity of fibula</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>external malleolus of fibula</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>fibular malleolus</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>lateral malleolus of fibula</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012320 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012320">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001637"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003502"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000974"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An artery of the neck.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:37075</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C52850</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C1707349</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>cervical artery</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012322 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012322">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012320"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The ascending cervical artery is a small branch which arises from the inferior thyroid artery as that vessel is passing behind the carotid sheath; it runs up on the anterior tubercles of the transverse processes of the cervical vertebrC&amp; in the interval between the Scalenus anterior and Longus capitis. To the muscles of the neck it gives twigs which anastomose with branches of the vertebral, and it sends one or two spinal branches into the vertebral canal through the intervertebral foramina to be distributed to the medulla spinalis and its membranes, and to the bodies of the vertebrC&amp;, in the same manner as the spinal branches from the vertebral. It anastomoses with the ascending pharyngeal and occipital arteries.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:52489</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:161846001</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Ascending_cervical_artery</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ascending cervical</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>ascending cervical artery</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012324 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012324">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012320"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The transverse cervical artery (transverse artery of neck, transversa colli artery) is a branch of the thyrocervical trunk, running at a higher level than the suprascapular artery.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:10664</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0001936</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:244224008</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Transverse_cervical_artery</OboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>cervical artery</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>cervical transverse artery</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>descending branch of the transverse cervical</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>transversalis artery colli</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>transversalis colli artery</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>transverse cervical</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>transverse cervical vessels</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>transverse cervical artery</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


