        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The joint that is formed by the union of the humerus, the scapula (or shoulder blade), and the clavicle (or collarbone). Commonly thought of as a single joint, the shoulder is actually made up of two separate joints - the glenohumeral and acromioclavicular joints.</obo:IAO_0000115>
