        <obo:IAO_0000115>The posterior intercostal arteries are a group of 11 paired segmental blood vessels that provide the primary arterial blood supply to the thoracic wall, intercostal muscles, overlying skin, parietal pleura, and structures surrounding the spinal cord. Source: Radiopaedia; https://radiopaedia.org/articles/posterior-intercostal-arteries</obo:IAO_0000115>
