                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_5006049"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A subdivision of the skeleton of the autopod consisting of the phalanges of digit 2 plus the associated metapodial element.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>this class represents a series of phalanges plus a metapodial element. In comparative anatomy terminology we would call this a &apos;digit&apos;, but the label &apos;digit&apos; is sometimes used to exclude metapodials and to include soft tissue. This series of elements is hypothesized to be homologous to radials.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>digit II digitopodial skeleton</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>digit 2</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>digit 2 skeleton</OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>digit 2 digitopodial skeleton</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


