    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0793723 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0793723">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001021"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The auriculotemporal nerve is a branch of the mandibular nerve (CN V3) that runs with the superficial temporal artery and vein, and provides sensory innervation to various regions on the side of the head, including parasympathetic innervation of the parotid gland (Adapted from Wikipedia)</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma53000"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0793723"/>
        <rdfs:label>Auriculotemporal nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794900 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794900">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001021"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Cutaneous nerve of the neck originating from nerve point of the neck and providing sensory innervation to skin over the clavicle, shoulder and chest. REVA annotation term.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794900"/>
        <rdfs:label>supraclavicular nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794951 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794951">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002386"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The lateral cutaneous nerve of forearm (or lateral antebrachial cutaneous nerve) is a sensory nerve representing the continuation of the musculocutaneous nerve beyond the lateral edge of the tendon of the biceps brachii muscle. The lateral antebrachial cutaneous nerve provides sensory innervation to the skin of the lateral forearm. It pierces the deep fascia of forearm to enter the subcutaneous compartment before splitting into a volar branch and a dorsal branch. It is derived from C5, C6 ventral rami.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002386"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794951"/>
        <rdfs:label>lateral cutaneous nerve of the forearm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794952 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794952">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003433"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The medial cutaneous nerve of the arm (also known as the medial brachial cutaneous nerve and the lesser internal cutaneous nerve) is a sensory branch of the medial cord of the brachial plexus derived from spinal nerves C8-T1. It provides sensory innervation to the lower portion of the medial arm. It descends accompanied by the basilic vein.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794952"/>
        <rdfs:label>Medial cutaneous nerve of the arm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794953 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794953">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003433"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The medial cutaneous nerve of the forearm (also known as the medial antebrachial cutaneous nerve) is a sensory branch of the medial cord of the brachial plexus derived from the ventral rami of spinal nerves C8-T1. It provides sensory innervation to the skin of the medial forearm.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003433"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794953"/>
        <rdfs:label>medial cutaneous nerve of the forearm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794954 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794954">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002398"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The dorsum of hand (dorsal area) is the corresponding area on the posterior part of the hand. This refers to the back of the hand, which is opposite of the palm side of the hand.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794954"/>
        <rdfs:label>dorsum of the hand</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794966 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794966">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794966"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A branch of the upper trunk of the brachial plexus (C5-C6) supplying the supraspinatus and infraspinatus muscles and contributing articular branches to the shoulder.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794966"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794966"/>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Nervus suprascapularis</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>suprascapular nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794967 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794967">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794977"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The continuation of the deep branch of the radial nerve after traversing the supinator muscle, supplying most extensor muscles of the forearm.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794977"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794967"/>
        <OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Posterior antebrachial interosseous nerve</OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>posterior interosseous nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794975 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794975">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794975"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The medial pectoral nerve (also known as the medial anterior thoracic nerve) is (typically) a branch of the medial cord of the brachial plexus and is derived from ventral rami  C8-T1. It provides motor innervation to the pectoralis minor muscle, and part of the pectoralis major muscle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794975"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794975"/>
        <rdfs:label>medial pectoral nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794977 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794977">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001492"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794977"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The radial nerve divides into a superficial (sensory) and deep (motor) branch at the cubital fossa. The deep branch of the radial nerve winds to the back of the forearm around the lateral side of the radius between the two planes of fibers of the supinator, and is prolonged downward between the superficial and deep layers of muscles, to the middle of the forearm. The deep branch and its continuation, called the posterior interosseous nerve, provides motor function to the muscles in the posterior compartment of the forearm, which are mostly the extensor muscles of the wrist and hand.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001492"/>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794977"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794977"/>
        <rdfs:label>deep branch of radial nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794979 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794979">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The dorsal scapular nerve is a branch of the brachial plexus, usually derived from the ventral ramus of cervical nerve C5. It provides motor innervation to the rhomboid major muscle, rhomboid minor muscle, and sometimes the levator scapulae muscle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001814"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794979"/>
        <rdfs:label>dorsal scapular nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794996 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794996">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034987"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The ilioinguinal nerve is a branch of the first lumbar nerve (L1). The ilioinguinal nerve then perforates the transversus abdominis near the anterior part of the iliac crest, and communicates with the iliohypogastric nerve between the transversus and the internal oblique muscle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034987"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794996"/>
        <rdfs:label>Ilioinguinal nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794999 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794999">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034987"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The lateral cutaneous nerve of the thigh (also called the lateral femoral cutaneous nerve) is a cutaneous nerve of the thigh. It originates from the second and third lumbar nerves which are derived from the lumbar plexus. It passes under the inguinal ligament to reach the thigh. It supplies sensation to the skin on the lateral part of the thigh by an anterior branch and a posterior branch. It is derived from the ventral rami of L2 and L3.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034987"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794999"/>
        <rdfs:label>Lateral cutaneous nerve of thigh</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795002">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034987"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The iliohypogastric nerve is a nerve that originates from the lumbar plexus that supplies sensation to skin over the lateral gluteal and hypogastric regions and motor to the internal oblique muscles and transverse abdominal muscles. It is derived from the ventral ramus of L1. It is a branch of the lumbar plexus that provides sensory innervation to the skin of the gluteal region and lower abdomen, as well as motor control to key muscles of the lower abdominal wall</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034987"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795002"/>
        <rdfs:label>iliohypogastric nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795005 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795005">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003433"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001492"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The posterior cutaneous nerve of arm (also known as posterior brachial cutaneous nerve) is a branch of the radial nerve that provides sensory innervation for much of the skin on the back of the arm. It is derived from the ventral rami of C5, C6, C7, and C8.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001492"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795005"/>
        <rdfs:label>Posterior cutaneous nerve of arm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795007 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795007">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0797544"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001493"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The superior lateral cutaneous nerve of arm (or superior lateral brachial cutaneous nerve) is the continuation of the posterior branch of the axillary nerve, after it pierces the deep fascia. It is derived from the ventral rami of C5 and C6.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001493"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795007"/>
        <rdfs:label>superior lateral cutaneous nerve of arm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795018 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795018">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001148"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Proper palmar digital nerves arise from the common digital branches of the median nerve and innervate the lateral 3 digits and the lateral side of the ring (4th) digit.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001148"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795018"/>
        <rdfs:label>proper palmar digital branches of median nerve</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795021 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795021">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0797544"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001492"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The inferior lateral cutaneous nerve of arm is a nerve found in humans and other animals. It is also called the inferior lateral brachial cutaneous nerve. It is a branch of the radial nerve that provides sensory and vasomotor innervation to the lower, lateral aspect of the arm.  It is derived from the ventral rami of C5 and C6.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001492"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795021"/>
        <rdfs:label>Inferior lateral cutaneous nerve of arm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795283 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795283">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012198"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001443"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The anatomical space between the first and second ribs, containing intercostal muscles, vessels, and nerves.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001443"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercostal_space</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma321185"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795283"/>
        <rdfs:label>first intercostal space</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795284 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795284">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004704"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001443"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A small triangular depression located inferior to the clavicle, bounded by the clavicle, deltoid, and pectoralis major muscles.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001443"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/infraclavicular-fossa-1536888660</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma61541"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795284"/>
        <rdfs:label>infraclavicular fossa</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006800"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000916"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A vertical line running along the midline of the anterior body surface, aligned with the sternum. On the anterior abdominal and chest walls, the anterior median line can be seen extending from the jugular notch, crossing over the sternum and linea alba in their midline, and reaching out to the midline pubic symphysis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000916"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/anterior-median-line-1536887700</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma20310"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285"/>
        <rdfs:label>anterior median line</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795286 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795286">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001062"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0008785"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A triangular region bounded by the clavicle superiorly, the pectoralis major medially, and the deltoid laterally.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0008785"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clavipectoral_triangle</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795286"/>
        <rdfs:label>clavipectoral triangle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795287 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795287">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001062"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001443"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The anterior boundary of the axilla, formed by the lower border of the pectoralis major muscle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001443"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/anterior-axillary-fold-1536887752</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma322184"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795287"/>
        <rdfs:label>anterior axillary fold</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795288 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795288">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001062"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0008785"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The posterior aspect of the wrist, containing the extensor tendons and underlying carpal bones.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0008785"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://www.uptodate.com/contents/anatomy-and-basic-biomechanics-of-the-wrist</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma24924"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795288"/>
        <rdfs:label>dorsal wrist</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795289 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795289">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004704"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001461"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The radial fossa, also called the anatomical snuffbox, is a triangular depression on the lateral wrist. It is bordered by the tendons of the extensor pollicis longus, extensor pollicis brevis, and abductor pollicis longus, with the scaphoid and trapezium forming its floor. It houses the radial artery and is clinically relevant for assessing scaphoid fractures or arterial pulse.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001461"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/radial-fossa-1537018612</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma23452"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795289"/>
        <rdfs:label>radial fossa</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795290 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795290">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000093"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A shallow groove extending from the lateral aspect of the nostril to the corner of the mouth.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/nasolabial-sulcus-1536888784</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma75018"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795290"/>
        <rdfs:label>nasolabial sulcus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795291 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795291">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001062"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003129"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The mandibular notch, also known as the sigmoid notch, is a groove in the ramus of the mandible. A curved depression between the coronoid and condylar processes of the mandible.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003129"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandibular_notch</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma59481"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795291"/>
        <rdfs:label>mandibular notch</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795292 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795292">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006800"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000033"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The demarcation at the anterior margin of the scalp where hair growth begins.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000033"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://www.semanticscholar.org/topic/Anterior-hairline/3368103</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma285414"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795292"/>
        <rdfs:label>anterior hairline</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795293 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795293">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004704"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000974"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A small depression located superior to the clavicle and medial to the clavicular head of the sternocleidomastoid muscle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000974"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/lesser-supraclavicular-fossa-1536888804</base:ilx_0777130>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma84981"/>
        <ilxtr:hasExistingId rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795293"/>
        <rdfs:label>lesser supraclavicular fossa</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795294 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795294">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004704"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000974"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The greater supraclavicular fossa refers to the larger, lateral depression above the clavicle, located lateral to the sternocleidomastoid muscle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <base:ilx_0112785 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000974"/>
        <base:ilx_0777130>https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/greater-supraclavicular-fossa-1536888404</base:ilx_0777130>
