        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 118. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridians. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <tara:hasChineseLabel>殷門(门)</tara:hasChineseLabel>
        <tara:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000376"/>
        <tara:hasIndicationsDescription>pain in the lower back and thigh, muscular atrophy, pain, numbness and motor impairment of the lower extremities, hemiplegia.</tara:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <tara:hasInnervationDescription>The posterior femoral cutaneous nerve; deeper, the sciatic nerve.</tara:hasInnervationDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>On the posterior aspect of the thigh, between the biceps femoris and the semitendinosus muscles, 6 B-cun inferior to the gluteal fold. Note 1: In the prone position, the semitendinosus and the biceps femoris muscles are more distinct when the knee is flexed against resistance. In addition, it is easier to find the two muscles with internal and external rotation of the hip. Note 2: 1 B-cun superior to the midpoint of the line connecting BL36 with BL40.</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 1.0-2.0 inches. Moxibustion is applicable.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
        <tara:hasPinyinLabel>Yinmen</tara:hasPinyinLabel>
        <tara:hasSpecificSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001374"/>
        <tara:hasSpecificSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001375"/>
        <tara:hasSpecificSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0036014"/>
        <tara:hasSynonym>B 37</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:hasSynonym>Bladder 37</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:hasSynonym>UB 37</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 37</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:hasVasculatureDescription>Laterally, the third perforating branches of the deep femoral artery and vein.</tara:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <tara:isLocatedOnMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <rdfs:label>BL 37</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


