        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 181. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridians. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <tara:hasChineseLabel>腦(脑,脳)空</tara:hasChineseLabel>
        <tara:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000033"/>
        <tara:hasIndicationsDescription>headache, stiffness of the neck, vertigo, painful eyes, tinnitus, epilepsy.</tara:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>On the head, at the same level as the supe- rior border of the external occipital protu- berance, directly superior to gB20. Note: GB19 is at the same level as GV17 and BL9.</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture subcutaneously 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
