        <dc:description>Represents a Crossing Point. Crossing points are those at the intersections of two or more meridians. Distributed mainly on the head, face and trunk, and amounting to over ninety in total. They are key points used to treat meridian disorders of the areas where they are located.</dc:description>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Ch. 6, An Introduction to Acupunture Points, Sec. III, Specific Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
