        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 154. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridians. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <tara:hasChineseLabel>內關(关,関)</tara:hasChineseLabel>
        <tara:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002386"/>
        <tara:hasIndicationsDescription>cardiac pain, palpitation, stuffy chest, pain in the hypochondriac region, stomachache, nausea, vomiting, hiccup, mental disorder, epilepsy, insomnia, febrile diseases, irritability, malaria, contracture and pain of the elbow and arm.</tara:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>On the anterior aspect of the forearm, between the tendons of the palmaris longus and the flexor carpi radialis, 2 B-cun proximal to the palmar wrist crease. Note 1: With the fist clenched, the wrist supinated and the elbow slightly flexed, the two tendons become more prominent. PC6 is located 2 B-cun proximal to PC7. the posterial point corresponding to PC6 is TE5. Note 2: If the palmaris longus tendon is not present, PC6 is medial to the flexor carpi radialis tendon.</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.8 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
        <tara:hasPinyinLabel>Neiguan</tara:hasPinyinLabel>
        <tara:hasSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6993030"/>
        <tara:hasSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_9493899"/>
        <tara:hasSpecificSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0016496"/>
        <tara:hasSpecificSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795334"/>
        <tara:hasSpecificSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795500"/>
        <tara:hasSynonym>P 6</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:hasSynonym>Pericardium 6</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:isLocatedOnMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4694897"/>
        <rdfs:label>PC 6</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


