                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 211. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <tara:hasChineseLabel>瘂(哑)門(门)</tara:hasChineseLabel>
        <tara:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000974"/>
        <tara:hasIndicationsDescription>mental disorder, epilepsy, deafness and mute, sudden hoarseness of the voice, apoplexy, stiffness of the tongue and aphasia, occipital headache, neck rigidity.</tara:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <tara:hasInnervationDescription>The third occipital nerve.</tara:hasInnervationDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>In the posterior region of the neck, in the depression superior to the spinous process of the second cervical vertebra (C2), on the posterior median line. Note: After locating GV16, GV15 is located 0.5 B-cun inferior to GV16.</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.8 inch. Neither upward obliquely nor deep puncture is advisable. It is near the medullary bulb in the deep layer, and the depth and angle of the puncture should be paid strict attention to.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
        <tara:hasPinyinLabel>Yamen</tara:hasPinyinLabel>
        <tara:hasSpecificSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001093"/>
        <tara:hasSpecificSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795312"/>
        <tara:hasSynonym>Du 15</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:hasSynonym>Governor Vessel 15</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:hasSynonym>VG 15</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of the occipital artery and vein.</tara:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <tara:isLocatedOnMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0386099"/>
        <rdfs:label>GV 15</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


