        <tara:hasIndicationsDescription>lower abdominal distension, retention of urine, edema, hernia, dysmenorrhea, sterility.</tara:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <tara:hasInnervationDescription>A branch of the subcostal nerve.</tara:hasInnervationDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>On the lower abdomen, 3 B-cun inferior to the centre of the umbilicus, 2 B-cun lateral to the anterior median line. Note: ST28 is 3 B-cun inferior to ST25, 1 B-cun inferior to St27, 2 B-cun lateral to CV4.</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.7-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
        <tara:hasPinyinLabel>Shuidao</tara:hasPinyinLabel>
