        <tara:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0016416"/>
        <tara:hasIndicationsDescription>pain in the hypochondriac region, vomiting, acid regurgitation, hiccup, jaundice, mastitis.</tara:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <tara:hasInnervationDescription>The seventh intercostal nerve.</tara:hasInnervationDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>In the anterior thoracic region, in the sev- enth intercostal space, 4 B-cun lateral to the anterior median line. Note 1: GB 24 is inferior to the centre of the nipple, one rib inferior to LR 14. Note 2: In females, GB24 can be found at the intersection of the midclavicular line and the seventh intercostal space.</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
