        <tara:hasIndicationsDescription>pain in the scapular region, numbness and aching of the upper extremities, motor impairment of the shoulder and arm.</tara:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <tara:hasInnervationDescription>The lateral suprascapular nerve and accessory nerve; deeper, the suprascapular nerve.</tara:hasInnervationDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>In the scapular region, in the supraspinatous fossa, superior to the midpoint of the spine of the scapula.</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.7 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
        <tara:hasPinyinLabel>Bingfeng</tara:hasPinyinLabel>
