        <tara:hasInnervationDescription>The posterior brachial cutaneous nerve and the muscular branch of the radial nerve.</tara:hasInnervationDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>On the posterior aspect of the elbow, in the depression 1 B-cun proximal to the prominence of the olecranon. Note: When the elbow is flexed, TE10 is located in the olecranon fossa.</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
        <tara:hasPinyinLabel>Tianjing</tara:hasPinyinLabel>
