        <tara:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002387"/>
        <tara:hasIndicationsDescription>facial or general edema, abdominal pain, borborygmus, swelling and pain of the dorsum of the foot.</tara:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <tara:hasInnervationDescription>The medial dorsal cu‚Ä¢ taneous nerve of foot.</tara:hasInnervationDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>On the dorsum of the foot, between the second and third metatarsal bones, in the depression proximal to the second metatarsophalangeal joint.</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
