        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Acupoint that hasSpecialPointRole some Special_Acupoint_Role.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description>Special points refer to the specific points of the fourteen meridians that have special properties and are grouped under special names. In view of their locations, they can be classified into two major groups: one on the limbs, and the other one on the head and the trunk.</dc:description>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation xml:lang="en">Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 6, An Introduction to Acupunture Points, Sec. III, Specific Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <tara:hasSynonym>Special Acupoint</tara:hasSynonym>
        <tara:hasSynonym>Special Acupuncture Point</tara:hasSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>Special Point</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


