        <tara:hasInnervationDescription>Superficially, the lateral branch of the posterior ramus of the second thoracic nerve, the accessory nerve; deeper, the muscular branch of the suprascapular nerve.</tara:hasInnervationDescription>
        <tara:hasLocationalDescription>In the scapular region, in the depression superior to the medial end of the spine of the scapula. Note: SI13 is located at the midpoint of the line connecting SI10 with the spinous pro- cess of the second thoracic vertebra (T2).</tara:hasLocationalDescription>
        <tara:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</tara:hasMethodDescription>
